WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:39.082
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:39.352 --> 00:43.064
‎DOCTOR X: MAFIA IN WHITE

3
00:43.147 --> 00:45.775
‎THIS DRAMA IS FICTITIOUS AND DIFFERS FROM ‎ACTUAL MEDICAL PRACTICES AND REGULATIONS.

4
00:45.859 --> 00:48.069
‎CHARACTERS AND SETTINGS ARE FICTIONAL. ‎CHILD ACTORS WERE FILMED SAFELY.

5
00:50.280 --> 00:53.032
‎The siblings lost their house ‎to a government airstrike

6
00:53.116 --> 00:54.200
‎along with their parents.

7
00:55.451 --> 00:57.162
‎They moved in with relatives,

8
00:57.245 --> 01:00.248
‎but civil war soon forced them ‎to flee again.

9
01:00.832 --> 01:04.002
‎Hold my hand tight and watch your step.

10
01:04.752 --> 01:06.713
‎After harrowing days ‎of wandering the streets,

11
01:06.796 --> 01:09.299
‎doing their best ‎to evade soldiers and looters

12
01:09.382 --> 01:12.802
‎-and scavenging through ruins to survive‎… ‎-Wow.

13
01:14.512 --> 01:15.430
‎Drink this.

14
01:15.930 --> 01:19.267
‎The two eventually collapsed ‎from malnutrition.

15
01:20.226 --> 01:22.145
‎Even as they lay there,

16
01:22.228 --> 01:24.981
‎they held hands, ‎refusing to give up on each other.

17
01:26.399 --> 01:30.194
‎And the White Wings Medical Corps ‎didn't give up on them either.

18
01:34.782 --> 01:35.617
‎Does it hurt?

19
01:35.700 --> 01:40.788
‎Dr. Kim Seung-hyo, a world-class surgeon ‎and distinguished medical professor,

20
01:41.748 --> 01:43.791
‎turned his back on wealth and fame

21
01:43.875 --> 01:47.503
‎to found the White Wings Medical Corps ‎and settle here in Lagota.

22
01:49.047 --> 01:50.757
‎His daughter also became a doctor,

23
01:50.840 --> 01:53.426
‎and even though ‎he was asked to return to Korea,

24
01:53.509 --> 01:56.471
‎he left everything behind ‎and went to Lagota.

25
01:57.180 --> 02:00.892
‎The greatest treasures in his simple life

26
02:01.392 --> 02:04.187
‎are these pictures drawn by the children.

27
02:04.270 --> 02:05.563
‎Baba.

28
02:05.647 --> 02:08.233
‎-The children call Dr. Kim "Baba." ‎-Thank you.

29
02:09.234 --> 02:11.694
‎Lagota's Baba, the white-coat hero.

30
02:12.195 --> 02:13.279
‎However,

31
02:13.363 --> 02:16.449
‎Baba Kim Seung-hyo can't do this alone.

32
02:16.532 --> 02:17.992
‎-Patient coming through. ‎-Clear the way.

33
02:18.076 --> 02:19.118
‎The civil war continues.

34
02:19.619 --> 02:22.789
‎-Let's get her to the treatment room. ‎-Medical supplies are dangerously low.

35
02:22.872 --> 02:26.334
‎Baba Kim Seung-hyo barely managed ‎to receive a heart transplant

36
02:26.417 --> 02:28.920
‎under these poor conditions.

37
02:29.504 --> 02:32.548
‎All the children prayed for Baba.

38
02:32.632 --> 02:34.259
‎-Baba! ‎-Baba!

39
02:34.342 --> 02:36.970
‎Please help the children of Lagota.

40
02:37.553 --> 02:41.182
‎Please become a baba for these children.

41
02:41.808 --> 02:44.102
‎Please help them continue to smile.

42
02:44.185 --> 02:45.561
‎CALL NOW TO DONATE 30,000 WON A MONTH

43
02:45.645 --> 02:48.648
‎DOCTOR X: MAFIA IN WHITE

44
02:50.191 --> 02:51.317
‎Okay, let's go.

45
02:51.401 --> 02:53.111
‎Time to go outside.

46
02:53.695 --> 02:56.364
‎-Neema, open. ‎-Good job.

47
03:03.121 --> 03:04.288
‎Teacher.

48
03:05.373 --> 03:06.249
‎Yes?

49
03:06.749 --> 03:07.875
‎Is Baba good?

50
03:08.501 --> 03:09.544
‎Good people?

51
03:11.921 --> 03:12.755
‎Right.

52
03:13.673 --> 03:16.217
‎He saved you,

53
03:16.300 --> 03:17.385
‎Neema,

54
03:17.468 --> 03:18.678
‎and your friends.

55
03:19.220 --> 03:20.596
‎He teaches you too.

56
03:22.056 --> 03:23.516
‎You said that yourself.

57
03:29.522 --> 03:30.356
‎Am I good?

58
03:31.065 --> 03:31.941
‎What about me?

59
03:32.734 --> 03:33.568
‎Hey.

60
03:38.031 --> 03:38.865
‎Baraka.

61
03:39.741 --> 03:40.575
‎Baraka!

62
03:46.039 --> 03:47.790
‎Na-gyeong!

63
03:50.335 --> 03:52.003
‎My family looks nothing alike, right?

64
03:52.837 --> 03:55.048
‎Gosh, I'm really bad at drawing.

65
03:56.883 --> 03:57.967
‎Won-jin.

66
03:58.718 --> 04:00.219
‎Your dad's a doctor.

67
04:00.803 --> 04:01.888
‎Yeah.

68
04:01.971 --> 04:05.099
‎So have you played doctor with him too?

69
04:05.725 --> 04:06.559
‎No.

70
04:07.143 --> 04:09.729
‎I got into big trouble with my mom

71
04:09.812 --> 04:11.773
‎when I picked up his stethoscope.

72
04:12.690 --> 04:15.902
‎And my dad's too busy to play with me.

73
04:15.985 --> 04:18.988
‎I know he's a great doctor and all, but…

74
04:19.072 --> 04:21.240
‎Hey, where are you going?

75
04:21.324 --> 04:22.408
‎Na-gyeong!

76
04:22.492 --> 04:24.327
‎MOM, DAD KIM SEUNG-HYO, KIM WON-JIN

77
04:37.590 --> 04:43.346
‎"PLAYING DOCTOR" ‎BY PARK TAE-GYEONG

78
04:48.810 --> 04:52.105
‎How about we go and play doctor now?

79
04:52.188 --> 04:53.481
‎PARK TAE-GYEONG

80
04:57.026 --> 05:00.655
‎"PLAYING DOCTOR" ‎BY PARK TAE-GYEONG

81
05:15.545 --> 05:16.587
‎No!

82
05:39.110 --> 05:41.195
‎GUSEO UNIVERSITY SEONAM MEDICAL CENTER

83
05:41.279 --> 05:42.405
‎It's been ages since we've seen

84
05:42.488 --> 05:45.366
‎Dr. Yoon from thoracic ‎and Dr. Sim from cardiology.

85
05:45.950 --> 05:48.327
‎Well, joint department meetings are rare.

86
05:49.996 --> 05:53.791
‎It's always tough going into briefings ‎on organ donation surgery.

87
05:53.875 --> 05:54.792
‎I agree.

88
05:56.460 --> 05:58.754
‎For his heart transplant,

89
05:58.838 --> 06:02.008
‎I heard Dr. Kim Seung-hyo ‎personally requested Gye Su-jeong.

90
06:02.091 --> 06:03.885
‎Apparently, she did his first transplant.

91
06:03.968 --> 06:05.052
‎I know.

92
06:05.136 --> 06:07.763
‎Who on earth is Gye Su-jeong?

93
06:07.847 --> 06:10.850
‎And he wants Dr. Jo ‎to be the anesthesiologist.

94
06:13.728 --> 06:14.937
‎Did you know, sir?

95
06:15.021 --> 06:17.440
‎That Dr. Jo is ‎Dr. Kim Seung-hyo's daughter?

96
06:17.523 --> 06:18.774
‎No.

97
06:19.525 --> 06:20.818
‎I had no idea.

98
06:20.902 --> 06:22.403
‎You didn't know either?

99
06:23.029 --> 06:25.448
‎I was actually wondering ‎if she was related to him.

100
06:26.490 --> 06:27.825
‎I'll have to ask her in a bit.

101
06:28.409 --> 06:31.037
‎Apparently, she changed her name ‎from Kim Won-jin.

102
06:31.120 --> 06:32.955
‎Everyone's talking about it.

103
06:33.039 --> 06:34.457
‎I'm sure she had her reasons.

104
06:35.082 --> 06:36.417
‎It's a re-dissection,

105
06:36.500 --> 06:38.753
‎so we need to make adjustments ‎to align with her surgical plan.

106
06:38.836 --> 06:40.254
‎I'll get on that, sir.

107
06:51.265 --> 06:54.143
‎Jeez, I can't ask her. ‎Why do they look so serious?

108
06:55.186 --> 06:56.812
‎I don't see Park Tae-gyeong either.

109
07:04.779 --> 07:06.030
‎Good job, Hyeon-a.

110
07:07.865 --> 07:08.991
‎It's healing well.

111
07:09.700 --> 07:12.286
‎Dr. Gye stopped by earlier

112
07:12.370 --> 07:13.871
‎and said the same thing.

113
07:15.081 --> 07:15.957
‎I see.

114
07:17.833 --> 07:19.460
‎Thank you.

115
07:19.544 --> 07:21.879
‎No, you should have it.

116
07:21.963 --> 07:24.131
‎Dr. Gye gave it to me.

117
07:24.715 --> 07:26.175
‎I have tons.

118
07:26.259 --> 07:28.177
‎You sure do. Good for you.

119
07:28.886 --> 07:30.596
‎Excuse me, Dr. Park.

120
07:30.680 --> 07:31.764
‎That famous doctor,

121
07:31.847 --> 07:34.267
‎the one who founded a relief organization…

122
07:34.350 --> 07:37.103
‎Dr. Kim Seung-hyo.

123
07:38.145 --> 07:39.897
‎Yes, him.

124
07:39.981 --> 07:43.484
‎Right now, ‎Hyeon-a wants to be like Dr. Gye,

125
07:43.568 --> 07:46.904
‎but her original dream ‎was to be like Dr. Kim Seung-hyo.

126
07:46.988 --> 07:49.991
‎I even sent donations to Baba ‎with my allowance money.

127
07:59.709 --> 08:01.460
‎Rock, paper, scissors.

128
08:02.628 --> 08:04.839
‎Hyeon-a really wants to meet him,

129
08:04.922 --> 08:08.301
‎saying he's a great doctor ‎for helping sick children overseas.

130
08:08.801 --> 08:10.928
‎She wants to wish him a quick recovery.

131
08:19.854 --> 08:20.938
‎Before we eat,

132
08:21.897 --> 08:23.149
‎let's play doctor.

133
08:31.657 --> 08:34.118
‎You can't tell your mom and dad, okay?

134
08:35.244 --> 08:36.412
‎Today,

135
08:37.246 --> 08:38.497
‎you'll be the doctor.

136
08:54.847 --> 08:55.973
‎Young doctor.

137
08:57.767 --> 08:59.101
‎Isn't it time to eat?

138
09:01.187 --> 09:03.064
‎I'm okay. Please excuse me.

139
09:04.398 --> 09:05.232
‎I'm the one

140
09:06.400 --> 09:08.569
‎who took Dr. Gye to Kim Seung-hyo.

141
09:17.119 --> 09:18.371
‎I wanted to show off.

142
09:20.873 --> 09:22.333
‎I wanted to show that great doctor

143
09:23.376 --> 09:25.670
‎how amazing my student was.

144
09:27.546 --> 09:29.256
‎I took her there to learn,

145
09:30.341 --> 09:32.426
‎but the fallout followed us here.

146
09:34.845 --> 09:35.680
‎So…

147
09:37.598 --> 09:38.849
‎why not resent me instead?

148
09:41.060 --> 09:42.645
‎Don't take it out on Su-jeong.

149
09:43.145 --> 09:45.940
‎She still has nightmares ‎and can't even open that child's letters.

150
09:47.024 --> 09:48.651
‎So take it out on me,

151
09:49.318 --> 09:50.986
‎Jang Hui-suk, the arrogant fool.

152
10:06.252 --> 10:10.798
‎He was my parents' ‎oldest and closest friend.

153
10:12.425 --> 10:14.093
‎He lived with us for a year

154
10:15.177 --> 10:17.388
‎while the new hospital was being built.

155
10:20.349 --> 10:21.767
‎By your logic,

156
10:22.351 --> 10:24.895
‎since my parents are the ones ‎who brought him to our home…

157
10:27.440 --> 10:29.775
‎then I should be upset with my parents.

158
10:32.486 --> 10:34.447
‎But my parents did nothing wrong.

159
10:36.615 --> 10:37.825
‎I know that much.

160
10:59.221 --> 11:02.099
‎Aunt, I have something to tell you.

161
11:02.183 --> 11:04.560
‎Did you operate on the patient ‎with the epidermoid cyst?

162
11:05.269 --> 11:06.353
‎Did you see it?

163
11:06.437 --> 11:09.857
‎You should've seen me ‎scoop out the tumor with a cup.

164
11:09.940 --> 11:10.775
‎A cup?

165
11:11.525 --> 11:12.359
‎Are you crazy?

166
11:14.361 --> 11:16.489
‎But Dr. Kim said ‎he did it back in the day.

167
11:17.114 --> 11:18.782
‎-What? ‎-That tumor

168
11:18.866 --> 11:21.494
‎had kept the patient ‎from sleeping on their back.

169
11:21.577 --> 11:23.621
‎Now they can, thanks to me.

170
11:23.704 --> 11:25.414
‎Do you know what they went through?

171
11:25.498 --> 11:28.000
‎You couldn't stop the bleeding, ‎and they kept passing out from the pain.

172
11:30.002 --> 11:30.836
‎But they were dying

173
11:31.879 --> 11:34.507
‎from late-stage cancer anyway. ‎I figured it was the least I could do.

174
11:34.590 --> 11:38.093
‎And not because Dr. Kim suggested ‎adding them to the Doctor X case logs?

175
11:39.595 --> 11:41.889
‎What's wrong, Aunt? ‎It was a new procedure--

176
11:41.972 --> 11:44.433
‎How do you know for sure ‎it was an epidermoid cyst?

177
11:45.184 --> 11:46.018
‎It was in the data.

178
11:46.101 --> 11:47.853
‎Was that really for the patient?

179
11:50.689 --> 11:54.026
‎Or was it to see if you could pull it off, ‎what the tumor looked like,

180
11:54.109 --> 11:55.778
‎what would happen if you cut into it,

181
11:55.861 --> 11:59.657
‎and how far you could push a surgery ‎without anesthesia?

182
12:01.158 --> 12:02.034
‎I mean…

183
12:03.744 --> 12:04.870
‎That's not why--

184
12:04.954 --> 12:06.705
‎You need to ask yourself.

185
12:07.206 --> 12:08.499
‎Was that surgery done

186
12:09.291 --> 12:11.585
‎solely and purely ‎in the patient's best interest?

187
12:36.110 --> 12:39.280
‎Teacher is really angry with me.

188
12:39.363 --> 12:40.197
‎Why?

189
12:49.498 --> 12:50.708
‎I guess I'm…

190
12:53.669 --> 12:54.628
‎a monster?

191
12:54.712 --> 12:55.796
‎No way!

192
12:55.879 --> 12:57.631
‎You're not a monster!

193
12:59.049 --> 13:00.175
‎Baraka.

194
13:00.259 --> 13:01.343
‎Monsters shoot.

195
13:01.427 --> 13:04.805
‎Monsters drop bombs. ‎Monsters fly airplanes.

196
13:05.848 --> 13:07.808
‎Su-jeong, you're not a monster.

197
13:09.476 --> 13:11.854
‎My dream is to be a doctor.

198
13:12.730 --> 13:14.690
‎Being like you is my dream.

199
13:15.190 --> 13:16.900
‎I want to become a doctor.

200
14:14.792 --> 14:15.876
‎You can go in.

201
14:18.295 --> 14:19.964
‎He's sleeping, so he won't even know.

202
14:22.383 --> 14:23.217
‎It's okay.

203
14:28.889 --> 14:29.848
‎You heard, right?

204
14:33.519 --> 14:35.437
‎About Park Tae-gyeong and the cushion.

205
14:37.022 --> 14:39.149
‎Dr. Gye saved his life again.

206
14:45.489 --> 14:47.032
‎While I just stood there watching.

207
14:53.330 --> 14:58.168
‎So these are the battle scars you got ‎while saving those children from the fire.

208
14:59.128 --> 15:01.714
‎People say these are proof…

209
15:04.758 --> 15:06.552
‎that you're an angel.

210
15:21.442 --> 15:23.027
‎Dr. Gye Su-jeong?

211
15:50.054 --> 15:51.388
‎It's been a long time, sir.

212
15:53.390 --> 15:54.433
‎Park Tae-gyeong?

213
15:54.933 --> 15:56.185
‎It's me, Tae-gyeong.

214
15:56.810 --> 15:58.145
‎Director Park Yun-il's son.

215
15:58.645 --> 16:00.105
‎I brought my sketchbook

216
16:00.898 --> 16:02.649
‎in case you forgot who I was.

217
16:03.609 --> 16:04.860
‎Do you want to see it?

218
16:10.240 --> 16:12.367
‎I drew pictures with you

219
16:13.160 --> 16:14.495
‎and practiced my handwriting.

220
16:22.211 --> 16:24.963
‎You told me to throw this away ‎because it was a secret.

221
16:26.340 --> 16:29.218
‎But I couldn't dare do it, ‎so I kept it well hidden.

222
16:30.719 --> 16:33.263
‎You said you wouldn't ‎treat my parents if they got sick,

223
16:34.389 --> 16:36.266
‎so I didn't tell anyone.

224
16:47.277 --> 16:49.571
‎I even drew pictures ‎from when we played doctor.

225
16:51.573 --> 16:54.785
‎So have you played doctor with him too?

226
17:04.920 --> 17:06.004
‎Na-gyeong!

227
17:13.220 --> 17:14.346
‎Na-gyeong…

228
17:22.104 --> 17:24.439
‎You can get clean.

229
17:26.024 --> 17:28.026
‎Remember what I told you in the ER

230
17:28.777 --> 17:29.945
‎when we ran into each other?

231
17:30.028 --> 17:31.488
‎I said now that we've reconnected,

232
17:31.989 --> 17:33.907
‎I could help you get clean.

233
17:34.533 --> 17:35.367
‎Remember?

234
17:38.912 --> 17:40.664
‎Please come down.

235
17:41.165 --> 17:45.377
‎Why won't you believe me?

236
17:46.044 --> 17:47.129
‎Na-gyeong, that's…

237
17:48.797 --> 17:51.758
‎Please get up here. I'm on the rooftop.

238
17:51.842 --> 17:53.135
‎It wasn't a hallucination.

239
17:55.596 --> 17:56.805
‎We played doctor.

240
17:57.723 --> 17:58.640
‎It happened.

241
18:01.727 --> 18:04.438
‎Whenever I slept over at your house‎…

242
18:06.106 --> 18:07.191
‎he gave me gifts.

243
18:09.359 --> 18:11.904
‎Let's go up to the room now.

244
18:13.155 --> 18:14.364
‎A secret‎…

245
18:15.365 --> 18:17.242
‎He said it was a secret.

246
18:17.326 --> 18:19.453
‎Okay, I hear you.

247
18:19.536 --> 18:21.830
‎I need you to get up here right now!

248
18:22.331 --> 18:23.332
‎Your mom…

249
18:25.000 --> 18:27.669
‎gave my mom money.

250
18:28.712 --> 18:29.588
‎What?

251
18:29.671 --> 18:31.089
‎You know,

252
18:32.841 --> 18:34.885
‎everyone says that your dad

253
18:34.968 --> 18:36.053
‎is an angel.

254
18:38.096 --> 18:39.014
‎Na-gyeong.

255
18:39.848 --> 18:41.725
‎It's the drugs talking right now.

256
18:41.808 --> 18:43.727
‎-You're just confused. ‎-Won-jin.

257
18:47.064 --> 18:47.940
‎I'm so happy

258
18:49.358 --> 18:52.444
‎to see you again.

259
18:53.737 --> 18:54.738
‎Good.

260
18:54.821 --> 18:56.281
‎Me too.

261
18:57.324 --> 18:59.743
‎So just take my hand and--

262
18:59.826 --> 19:01.536
‎I'm so happy that I can show you.

263
19:04.164 --> 19:05.040
‎Watch closely.

264
19:06.291 --> 19:07.459
‎Your dad…

265
19:10.045 --> 19:11.129
‎is a monster.

266
19:46.415 --> 19:47.791
‎A long time ago,

267
19:48.834 --> 19:50.919
‎my dad said you'd come here ‎for your transplant

268
19:51.003 --> 19:52.629
‎if a donor became available.

269
19:54.214 --> 19:55.841
‎That's why I chose to intern here.

270
19:57.217 --> 19:59.678
‎Because I had to ask you something.

271
20:05.475 --> 20:06.310
‎Sir?

272
20:23.327 --> 20:24.536
‎You look so peaceful.

273
21:23.929 --> 21:26.139
‎Excuse me. Are you okay?

274
21:26.848 --> 21:27.933
‎Oh, Ms. Jang!

275
21:28.683 --> 21:29.893
‎Let me help you up.

276
21:30.685 --> 21:32.396
‎Tell me what's wrong.

277
21:32.979 --> 21:34.773
‎Let me take you to the ER.

278
21:36.858 --> 21:38.652
‎-I'm okay. ‎-No, you're not.

279
21:38.735 --> 21:41.655
‎I've never abandoned a patient ‎who needs help.

280
21:41.738 --> 21:43.865
‎You can't go. ‎You're having trouble breathing.

281
21:44.449 --> 21:45.450
‎Lean on me.

282
21:46.785 --> 21:47.702
‎Dr. Kim.

283
21:48.829 --> 21:50.622
‎You're such a good doctor.

284
21:50.705 --> 21:51.540
‎Me?

285
21:51.623 --> 21:52.624
‎Of course, I am.

286
21:53.917 --> 21:56.294
‎So lean on me, and let's go in.

287
21:56.795 --> 22:00.006
‎You hyperventilated a bit, ‎so let's get you checked out.

288
22:00.590 --> 22:01.425
‎Here.

289
22:02.217 --> 22:03.593
‎This is for you.

290
22:05.971 --> 22:07.097
‎What is it?

291
22:07.180 --> 22:08.890
‎You get to have it today.

292
22:08.974 --> 22:10.475
‎Please enjoy it,

293
22:10.559 --> 22:12.561
‎and take good care of your patients.

294
22:12.644 --> 22:15.397
‎But I don't have any patients ‎because the ER is closed.

295
22:15.480 --> 22:17.065
‎-I can't take this-- ‎-Goodbye.

296
22:17.566 --> 22:18.400
‎But…

297
22:19.401 --> 22:20.444
‎You're okay, right?

298
22:43.300 --> 22:45.719
‎He's dependent on pain medication,

299
22:45.802 --> 22:47.637
‎so he can't hear anything anyway.

300
22:47.721 --> 22:49.264
‎And he won't remember what happened.

301
22:54.644 --> 22:56.730
‎I wish we could do the same.

302
23:11.369 --> 23:14.414
‎Why are you looking at me like that?

303
23:16.166 --> 23:17.167
‎Dr. Gye.

304
23:19.586 --> 23:20.462
‎Is it true?

305
23:22.172 --> 23:23.965
‎Were there other children too?

306
23:55.288 --> 23:57.040
‎-Ms. Jang. ‎-You're home.

307
23:58.208 --> 23:59.793
‎-Eung-gu, get her some water. ‎-Okay.

308
24:00.835 --> 24:01.753
‎Where's Su-jeong?

309
24:02.587 --> 24:03.838
‎I didn't see her.

310
24:04.547 --> 24:05.757
‎You didn't?

311
24:06.341 --> 24:07.425
‎Or you couldn't?

312
24:12.889 --> 24:14.057
‎I didn't have the energy

313
24:14.808 --> 24:17.894
‎after seeing the young doctor and Dr. Jo.

314
24:20.981 --> 24:21.940
‎Oh dear.

315
24:23.066 --> 24:24.025
‎Here we go.

316
24:33.201 --> 24:35.829
‎There's no way this is just for me.

317
24:35.912 --> 24:37.789
‎I have a feeling it's a feast

318
24:37.872 --> 24:41.126
‎Ms. Jang prepared ‎to feed you and a couple of others.

319
24:42.836 --> 24:45.213
‎Wow, I've never seen you

320
24:45.297 --> 24:47.549
‎this calm around food.

321
24:47.632 --> 24:49.509
‎Something is definitely wrong.

322
24:50.385 --> 24:51.219
‎No, there isn't.

323
24:51.303 --> 24:53.013
‎Did you just pick up chopsticks?

324
24:53.096 --> 24:55.432
‎Chopsticks are for nibbling. ‎Where's your spoon?

325
24:55.515 --> 24:57.976
‎This isn't like you. What's going on?

326
25:01.146 --> 25:02.564
‎No, no.

327
25:02.647 --> 25:03.982
‎I was just kidding.

328
25:04.065 --> 25:05.775
‎You should've clocked out by now,

329
25:05.859 --> 25:08.903
‎but you're roaming the hospital ‎like a stray cat.

330
25:09.404 --> 25:10.989
‎So like a good cat caregiver,

331
25:11.072 --> 25:12.866
‎I'm taking you in ‎and feeding you right meow.

332
25:13.450 --> 25:14.367
‎Meow.

333
25:16.161 --> 25:17.078
‎Pretty good, right?

334
25:17.162 --> 25:18.747
‎Let's eat.

335
25:22.500 --> 25:26.463
‎I saw Ms. Jang earlier today ‎stumbling near the lobby

336
25:26.546 --> 25:28.173
‎and breathing heavily.

337
25:29.924 --> 25:30.759
‎Like this.

338
25:32.052 --> 25:34.637
‎Luckily, she got better and went home.

339
25:40.101 --> 25:41.019
‎You know,

340
25:42.312 --> 25:44.606
‎an ordinary guy like me

341
25:44.689 --> 25:46.775
‎can't even begin to imagine

342
25:47.442 --> 25:50.278
‎how you and Ms. Jang ‎have managed to make it this far.

343
25:50.779 --> 25:53.865
‎Or how Buzzkill Jo Won-jin ‎used to be Kim Won-jin.

344
25:53.948 --> 25:56.826
‎How could she not tell me? ‎It makes me feel so left out.

345
25:56.910 --> 25:57.744
‎Seriously.

346
25:59.371 --> 26:02.457
‎And I don't know why Tae-gyeong, ‎that oh-so-cheerful fool,

347
26:02.540 --> 26:04.793
‎just disappeared from your side.

348
26:08.213 --> 26:10.256
‎But I do know this.

349
26:12.300 --> 26:14.052
‎I know you're all doing your best

350
26:14.135 --> 26:16.346
‎not to fall apart.

351
26:23.269 --> 26:25.271
‎I can see that in this this meal.

352
26:26.106 --> 26:29.734
‎Ms. Jang made it with the desire ‎to help you stay strong.

353
26:29.818 --> 26:31.653
‎And her own desire to stay strong.

354
26:34.114 --> 26:35.115
‎Dr. Gye.

355
26:38.576 --> 26:39.577
‎Don't fall apart.

356
26:40.537 --> 26:41.621
‎For Ms. Jang's sake.

357
26:43.832 --> 26:44.999
‎Man…

358
26:45.917 --> 26:48.086
‎This kind of rice takes a lot of work.

359
26:48.169 --> 26:49.629
‎It's nutritious steamed rice.

360
26:52.132 --> 26:53.425
‎It was cooked in a stone pot.

361
26:55.844 --> 26:59.055
‎Buzzkill Won-jin and MIA Tae-gyeong ‎should be eating with us.

362
26:59.597 --> 27:01.141
‎Where are they?

363
27:06.479 --> 27:08.231
‎ONYU NURSING HOME

364
27:20.910 --> 27:22.912
‎It's strange. She never throws that.

365
27:22.996 --> 27:23.955
‎She wipes it every day.

366
27:24.706 --> 27:27.625
‎Her dementia makes her ‎forgetful and clumsy,

367
27:27.709 --> 27:29.627
‎but she always leaves that photo alone.

368
27:30.462 --> 27:31.421
‎Isn't it remarkable?

369
27:33.298 --> 27:35.758
‎Come often. You don't visit enough.

370
27:53.318 --> 27:54.903
‎How?

371
27:55.570 --> 27:58.114
‎How? Tell me how!

372
27:58.198 --> 27:59.449
‎How could he?

373
28:04.204 --> 28:06.539
‎He stopped after I found out.

374
28:07.499 --> 28:09.876
‎I apologized to Na-gyeong,

375
28:09.959 --> 28:12.295
‎and then her mom asked for money--

376
28:12.378 --> 28:15.798
‎Do you call that an excuse?

377
28:19.093 --> 28:20.011
‎Your dad…

378
28:22.013 --> 28:23.389
‎He has a disease.

379
28:24.641 --> 28:25.475
‎What?

380
28:25.558 --> 28:29.479
‎God gave him the disease as a test.

381
28:30.355 --> 28:31.481
‎Is that what he said?

382
28:32.565 --> 28:33.858
‎Your dad is a great angel.

383
28:34.776 --> 28:37.070
‎Even now, he's in that faraway place

384
28:37.153 --> 28:40.073
‎caring for those in pain ‎and expecting nothing in return.

385
28:41.032 --> 28:43.243
‎He's serving as a good shepherd ‎to the lost sheep--

386
28:43.326 --> 28:44.786
‎Dad is…

387
28:47.247 --> 28:48.957
‎Dad is a monster!

388
28:51.876 --> 28:52.836
‎Won-jin.

389
28:54.754 --> 28:55.713
‎How could you…

390
28:57.715 --> 28:58.758
‎call him that?

391
29:00.885 --> 29:03.513
‎Your dad isn't like that anymore!

392
29:07.475 --> 29:08.852
‎Has it ever occurred to you

393
29:09.477 --> 29:12.272
‎that your dad might have done that

394
29:12.355 --> 29:15.567
‎to spare you from the test he was given?

395
29:29.247 --> 29:30.081
‎Mom.

396
29:32.542 --> 29:33.376
‎Mom…

397
29:36.713 --> 29:38.006
‎You're a monster too.

398
29:40.383 --> 29:42.135
‎We're never going back to that photo.

399
29:44.178 --> 29:45.722
‎I'm no longer your daughter.

400
29:50.351 --> 29:52.687
‎Why did you come here ‎instead of the police?

401
29:53.897 --> 29:56.024
‎You could've told them what he did.

402
29:56.107 --> 29:57.567
‎So why did you come here first?

403
30:02.113 --> 30:04.657
‎It's because you want to believe him.

404
30:05.825 --> 30:06.784
‎Won-jin.

405
30:07.785 --> 30:11.080
‎Now that you know the truth, ‎we just need to believe it.

406
30:12.665 --> 30:13.917
‎Right, Won-jin?

407
30:44.989 --> 30:51.996
‎INTERN, KIM WON-JIN

408
31:12.976 --> 31:15.645
‎Darn it, they need to pay you overtime.

409
31:16.437 --> 31:17.313
‎It's so late…

410
31:17.814 --> 31:18.731
‎Goodness.

411
31:19.607 --> 31:20.817
‎Where's your umbrella?

412
31:21.317 --> 31:22.318
‎My word.

413
31:23.444 --> 31:25.279
‎Have you eaten yet?

414
31:28.324 --> 31:29.409
‎That's…

415
31:31.244 --> 31:33.621
‎Come here. You're soaking wet.

416
31:39.460 --> 31:40.503
‎Aunt.

417
31:41.045 --> 31:42.213
‎Why did you take me in?

418
31:43.715 --> 31:44.590
‎What do you mean?

419
31:47.218 --> 31:49.512
‎This won't do. Go and get changed.

420
31:50.304 --> 31:52.265
‎I'll have some hot ginger tea ready.

421
31:52.974 --> 31:54.976
‎Hurry. You'll catch a cold.

422
31:58.146 --> 31:58.980
‎Tell me.

423
32:00.481 --> 32:02.191
‎You're not even my real aunt.

424
32:05.695 --> 32:07.780
‎I asked your mom that same question.

425
32:09.157 --> 32:10.199
‎"In-ok."

426
32:10.783 --> 32:12.410
‎"Why did you take me in?"

427
32:13.786 --> 32:15.121
‎"You're not even my real sister."

428
32:17.540 --> 32:18.750
‎What did she say?

429
32:20.418 --> 32:21.711
‎"I don't know."

430
32:21.794 --> 32:23.713
‎"The moment I saw you,

431
32:23.796 --> 32:25.214
‎I just wanted to take you home,

432
32:26.549 --> 32:28.885
‎bathe you in warm water,

433
32:29.427 --> 32:30.928
‎feed you a warm meal,

434
32:31.429 --> 32:34.807
‎and give you a warm bed. ‎That's all I could think of."

435
32:35.308 --> 32:36.225
‎That's what she said.

436
32:37.268 --> 32:38.811
‎I didn't understand at first.

437
32:41.314 --> 32:43.066
‎Remember how I was late…

438
32:44.984 --> 32:46.360
‎to her funeral?

439
32:46.444 --> 32:47.945
‎THE LATE KANG IN-OK

440
32:52.200 --> 32:53.242
‎All I wanted

441
32:53.826 --> 32:56.245
‎was to bathe you in warm water,

442
32:56.996 --> 32:58.623
‎feed you a warm meal,

443
32:59.123 --> 33:00.750
‎and give you a warm bed.

444
33:01.250 --> 33:03.169
‎That's all I could think of.

445
33:04.879 --> 33:05.963
‎That's just life.

446
33:06.798 --> 33:08.007
‎You know?

447
33:16.307 --> 33:17.433
‎I wanted to do the same.

448
33:20.645 --> 33:21.938
‎For Baraka,

449
33:23.856 --> 33:24.732
‎Neema…

450
33:27.985 --> 33:30.446
‎and all of the children I met back then.

451
33:44.460 --> 33:45.711
‎The bulgogi was good.

452
34:37.763 --> 34:39.849
‎GUSEO UNIVERSITY SEONAM MEDICAL CENTER

453
34:40.433 --> 34:42.935
‎He went to get examined.

454
34:43.019 --> 34:44.020
‎I see.

455
34:44.103 --> 34:46.564
‎He missed you a lot.

456
34:48.316 --> 34:50.902
‎You look even more like him in person ‎than in the photo.

457
35:56.342 --> 35:57.218
‎What brings you here?

458
35:58.594 --> 35:59.595
‎Is this it?

459
36:00.221 --> 36:01.514
‎The album you saw that day?

460
36:03.057 --> 36:03.891
‎Is this it?

461
36:27.790 --> 36:30.376
‎Excuse me, but did you see…

462
36:36.382 --> 36:38.009
‎He brought this here.

463
36:38.092 --> 36:38.926
‎He brought…

464
36:40.177 --> 36:41.178
‎How dare he?

465
36:44.307 --> 36:46.142
‎What…

466
36:47.685 --> 36:48.602
‎Look, it's Dr. Gye.

467
36:48.686 --> 36:50.021
‎Dr. Gye!

468
36:57.695 --> 36:58.696
‎Hyeon-a…

469
37:00.406 --> 37:02.366
‎She wanted to meet him.

470
37:07.496 --> 37:09.332
‎She said he told her to come.

471
37:15.421 --> 37:16.255
‎Dr. Gye.

472
37:24.680 --> 37:25.514
‎Just this once…

473
37:29.477 --> 37:31.604
‎Could you fail?

474
37:37.568 --> 37:38.986
‎Just this once.

475
37:41.197 --> 37:42.782
‎Could you please fail?

476
38:16.148 --> 38:17.441
‎Hi, Neema.

477
38:19.026 --> 38:21.237
‎I'm sorry it took so long to write back.

478
38:23.906 --> 38:26.242
‎I just didn't have the courage.

479
38:32.373 --> 38:33.207
‎To be honest…

480
38:35.334 --> 38:36.544
‎I'm a coward.

481
38:37.711 --> 38:39.713
‎I'm not brave enough to read your letters.

482
38:42.425 --> 38:43.300
‎But…

483
38:43.926 --> 38:45.302
‎I always think about you

484
38:45.928 --> 38:47.263
‎and wonder how you're doing.

485
38:50.307 --> 38:51.183
‎Neema.

486
38:52.268 --> 38:53.769
‎What do you like now?

487
38:55.980 --> 38:57.356
‎What songs do you sing?

488
38:59.400 --> 39:02.820
‎Does Baraka appear in your dreams?

489
39:05.656 --> 39:06.949
‎Teacher!

490
39:08.659 --> 39:09.952
‎Neema.

491
39:14.957 --> 39:16.417
‎Wow.

492
39:16.500 --> 39:18.502
‎It's so pretty.

493
39:21.464 --> 39:23.924
‎Baraka, bum cream. No, no.

494
39:25.634 --> 39:27.344
‎Baraka is going to get in trouble.

495
39:28.429 --> 39:30.806
‎Night, every day. To Baba.

496
39:31.390 --> 39:32.475
‎He's not getting better.

497
39:33.058 --> 39:34.018
‎To Baba?

498
39:34.810 --> 39:36.353
‎Every day? At night?

499
39:38.481 --> 39:39.648
‎Doctor play.

500
39:42.776 --> 39:43.694
‎They play doctor?

501
39:56.832 --> 39:58.250
‎Doctor. Study.

502
39:59.502 --> 40:01.045
‎They said no.

503
40:01.545 --> 40:02.713
‎I can't.

504
40:05.132 --> 40:06.133
‎I see.

505
40:08.302 --> 40:09.845
‎Some kids can't sleep

506
40:09.929 --> 40:11.639
‎because of nightmares.

507
40:12.806 --> 40:15.768
‎So they feel better ‎when they sleep with Baba.

508
40:16.602 --> 40:17.520
‎Really?

509
40:18.312 --> 40:19.146
‎Why?

510
40:20.481 --> 40:21.315
‎It's nothing.

511
40:24.193 --> 40:26.403
‎We raised so much money this time

512
40:26.487 --> 40:28.822
‎that we can cover the cost ‎of all our medical supplies.

513
40:29.406 --> 40:30.866
‎Everyone's relieved

514
40:30.950 --> 40:32.952
‎since the kids have nowhere else to go.

515
40:52.054 --> 40:53.973
‎Is there somewhere else we could go?

516
40:54.848 --> 40:56.392
‎What do you mean?

517
40:56.475 --> 40:57.851
‎I don't know.

518
40:57.935 --> 41:01.855
‎There's nowhere else ‎we could go, is there?

519
41:03.691 --> 41:05.651
‎-It's Baba. ‎-Baba.

520
41:05.734 --> 41:07.069
‎Good day, Baba.

521
41:07.152 --> 41:09.363
‎-Baba! ‎-Hello.

522
41:09.446 --> 41:10.656
‎Good day.

523
41:10.739 --> 41:11.657
‎Hello.

524
41:44.607 --> 41:46.650
‎We're on patrol tonight, right?

525
41:46.734 --> 41:49.278
‎Get some more sleep. ‎I'll go to the clinic.

526
41:49.361 --> 41:52.114
‎No, it's okay. Oh my goodness…

527
41:53.407 --> 41:54.658
‎It's fine.

528
41:58.329 --> 42:00.205
‎Why does my body feel so heavy?

529
42:04.168 --> 42:05.586
‎I hope these fit him.

530
42:05.669 --> 42:06.587
‎They will.

531
42:06.670 --> 42:09.340
‎After everything you did ‎to get them, they will.

532
42:10.966 --> 42:11.842
‎Su-jeong.

533
42:12.509 --> 42:13.969
‎I'll be there in 30 minutes.

534
42:30.361 --> 42:33.238
‎Baraka and Neema. Where are you?

535
42:56.595 --> 42:57.888
‎Neema.

536
42:59.765 --> 43:00.641
‎Neema.

537
43:02.518 --> 43:03.477
‎Neema!

538
43:40.806 --> 43:41.640
‎Baraka?

539
43:43.892 --> 43:44.727
‎Neema?

540
45:12.439 --> 45:13.857
‎Is Baba good?

541
45:13.941 --> 45:15.317
‎Good people?

542
45:23.784 --> 45:24.701
‎Please…

543
45:26.119 --> 45:27.913
‎Is there somewhere else we could go?

544
45:29.248 --> 45:30.541
‎What do you mean?

545
45:31.458 --> 45:32.334
‎I don't know.

546
45:32.417 --> 45:36.463
‎There's nowhere else ‎we could go, is there?

547
46:15.377 --> 46:17.379
‎-Hurry, outside! Go! ‎-Careful!

548
46:17.462 --> 46:18.463
‎Neema!

549
46:18.547 --> 46:19.923
‎Baraka!

550
46:21.675 --> 46:22.634
‎Neema!

551
46:23.594 --> 46:24.553
‎Baraka!

552
46:26.597 --> 46:27.639
‎Baraka!

553
46:28.682 --> 46:29.558
‎Neema!

554
46:31.143 --> 46:31.977
‎Baraka!

555
46:34.646 --> 46:35.480
‎Neema.

556
46:37.107 --> 46:38.483
‎Teacher…

557
46:40.193 --> 46:41.153
‎Let's go.

558
46:49.036 --> 46:49.995
‎Su-jeong!

559
46:56.460 --> 46:58.420
‎Baraka. Where's Baraka?

560
47:19.524 --> 47:21.443
‎Don't make me start a fire.

561
47:21.526 --> 47:25.155
‎Teacher, please leave us alone.

562
47:26.615 --> 47:28.408
‎Poor Baraka.

563
47:39.503 --> 47:40.504
‎Neema.

564
47:41.254 --> 47:42.839
‎You're still outside the door.

565
47:48.178 --> 47:49.638
‎Run, Neema!

566
47:53.392 --> 47:54.351
‎Baraka!

567
48:02.150 --> 48:03.360
‎Baraka!

568
48:15.038 --> 48:15.872
‎Baraka!

569
48:17.958 --> 48:18.959
‎Baraka!

570
48:19.918 --> 48:20.794
‎Baraka!

571
48:33.432 --> 48:34.266
‎Baraka.

572
49:07.257 --> 49:08.258
‎Wait…

573
49:33.867 --> 49:34.785
‎No.

574
49:48.590 --> 49:49.466
‎Baraka.

575
49:52.511 --> 49:54.429
‎One, two, three, four…

576
49:54.513 --> 49:55.388
‎Baraka.

577
49:59.059 --> 50:00.477
‎One, two, three, four…

578
50:12.572 --> 50:13.573
‎Baraka.

579
50:14.074 --> 50:14.908
‎Baraka?

580
50:15.992 --> 50:16.910
‎Wake up.

581
50:18.411 --> 50:19.412
‎Baraka…

582
50:57.492 --> 50:59.035
‎No matter how long I wait…

583
50:59.995 --> 51:01.663
‎No!

584
51:04.916 --> 51:07.002
‎…Baraka doesn't appear in my dreams.

585
51:22.934 --> 51:23.894
‎That makes all dreams

586
51:24.686 --> 51:26.438
‎excruciating for me.

587
51:26.521 --> 51:28.481
‎We removed all items of concern.

588
51:29.316 --> 51:30.275
‎The children…

589
51:30.859 --> 51:33.570
‎Yes, we're still looking for Neema.

590
51:34.279 --> 51:37.073
‎We'll handle everything ‎so it won't affect Baba.

591
51:50.253 --> 51:51.963
‎We asked Mi-gyeong for help

592
51:52.631 --> 51:54.758
‎to find you a foster family.

593
51:56.259 --> 51:57.135
‎And then…

594
51:59.095 --> 52:00.305
‎I ran away.

595
52:01.389 --> 52:02.724
‎To another place.

596
52:02.807 --> 52:05.602
‎LAW

597
52:07.479 --> 52:09.189
‎It's your turn next.

598
52:17.906 --> 52:20.408
‎That settles the old debt I owed you ‎for saving my life.

599
52:20.492 --> 52:23.161
‎It was nice seeing you again. ‎You're welcome here anytime.

600
52:23.244 --> 52:24.120
‎But…

601
52:24.955 --> 52:27.415
‎Dr. Jang Hui-suk didn't give up on me.

602
52:37.217 --> 52:38.259
‎Let's go home, Su-jeong.

603
52:39.761 --> 52:40.637
‎Home…

604
52:41.262 --> 52:43.306
‎Do I even deserve to have one?

605
52:45.266 --> 52:46.393
‎Do I deserve to eat

606
52:47.435 --> 52:48.937
‎and find the strength to go on?

607
52:51.523 --> 52:52.357
‎Here.

608
52:58.071 --> 52:59.948
‎I know you went there to die.

609
53:00.448 --> 53:02.283
‎Do you think I'll let that happen?

610
53:04.744 --> 53:05.662
‎Eat.

611
53:06.287 --> 53:07.706
‎Eat this right now.

612
53:09.290 --> 53:10.917
‎Open your mouth.

613
53:16.131 --> 53:17.048
‎Aunt.

614
53:19.926 --> 53:20.802
‎We…

615
53:22.887 --> 53:26.307
‎saved that person.

616
53:30.270 --> 53:31.104
‎What?

617
53:31.604 --> 53:32.439
‎We…

618
53:33.773 --> 53:35.358
‎saved that person…

619
53:39.529 --> 53:40.697
‎and felt happy.

620
53:42.949 --> 53:43.867
‎We…

621
53:45.160 --> 53:46.619
‎were glad…

622
53:49.873 --> 53:50.874
‎that he survived.

623
53:55.003 --> 53:56.129
‎We…

624
53:57.297 --> 53:59.215
‎saved that person…

625
54:01.718 --> 54:03.511
‎and laughed!

626
54:13.188 --> 54:14.189
‎I'm sorry.

627
54:17.567 --> 54:19.277
‎I'm sorry we saved that person.

628
54:19.903 --> 54:21.196
‎I'm sorry we saved him,

629
54:21.946 --> 54:24.616
‎laughed, and felt happy about it.

630
54:25.575 --> 54:26.910
‎I'm sorry I didn't know.

631
54:27.869 --> 54:29.871
‎I'm sorry I couldn't save Baraka.

632
54:30.580 --> 54:32.332
‎Just one bite.

633
54:34.084 --> 54:35.043
‎I'm sorry.

634
54:35.627 --> 54:36.753
‎-Come on. ‎-I'm sorry.

635
54:38.463 --> 54:39.923
‎I'm sorry for being alive.

636
54:46.805 --> 54:48.056
‎Neema…

637
54:48.848 --> 54:49.849
‎sent you a letter.

638
54:52.477 --> 54:55.855
‎She's doing well at her new home.

639
54:58.942 --> 54:59.901
‎A letter?

640
55:01.569 --> 55:03.029
‎Then Neema can…

641
55:03.113 --> 55:04.572
‎She learned how to read and write.

642
55:04.656 --> 55:06.366
‎She knows how to write now.

643
55:18.920 --> 55:19.963
‎Neema sent this…

644
55:21.798 --> 55:22.882
‎to protect you.

645
55:52.620 --> 55:53.788
‎Su-jeong?

646
55:54.455 --> 55:56.332
‎-Ms. Jang! ‎-Blessing and grace.

647
55:56.416 --> 55:58.293
‎-Mi-gyeong! Get down here! ‎-Baraka and Neema.

648
55:59.836 --> 56:00.670
‎My friends.

649
56:01.796 --> 56:03.214
‎My saviors.

650
56:04.841 --> 56:05.717
‎Dr. Gye.

651
56:06.759 --> 56:08.803
‎Please. Just this once.

652
56:10.763 --> 56:12.307
‎Could you please fail?

653
56:53.348 --> 56:54.474
‎Do you have dreams too?

654
56:57.852 --> 56:58.770
‎Nightmares?

655
57:13.743 --> 57:14.744
‎But…

656
57:18.456 --> 57:19.749
‎you were all alone.

657
57:57.203 --> 58:01.416
‎I'm going to save that person again.

658
58:10.216 --> 58:12.969
‎That monster who buried his face

659
58:14.178 --> 58:15.763
‎in Baraka's chest

660
58:16.806 --> 58:18.433
‎to survive the flames.

661
58:21.019 --> 58:23.229
‎That monster who took away your voice.

662
58:30.987 --> 58:32.697
‎I'm going to save him.

663
58:46.502 --> 58:49.881
‎He'll get a new heart

664
58:51.049 --> 58:52.759
‎and look for ways to be around children,

665
58:53.593 --> 58:55.803
‎and his followers ‎will keep covering for him.

666
58:57.180 --> 58:59.182
‎And then one day,

667
58:59.891 --> 59:00.850
‎he'll die peacefully,

668
59:01.768 --> 59:04.729
‎mourned and respected by all.

669
59:06.272 --> 59:09.275
‎But that's too easy.

670
59:10.401 --> 59:11.486
‎That's too…

671
59:12.820 --> 59:13.988
‎good for him.

672
59:14.614 --> 59:16.991
‎PATIENT: KIM SEUNG-HYO ‎PRIMARY SURGEON: GYE SU-JEONG

673
59:56.280 --> 59:57.198
‎Everyone.

674
59:58.449 --> 59:59.283
‎A moment of silence.

675
01:00:02.870 --> 01:00:05.540
‎We honor the donor and their family,

676
01:00:05.623 --> 01:00:07.375
‎whose choice was a beginning, not an end.

677
01:00:07.458 --> 01:00:08.876
‎My last patient‎…

678
01:00:09.627 --> 01:00:10.878
‎Yes, understood.

679
01:00:13.548 --> 01:00:14.841
‎They're putting the donor under.

680
01:00:14.924 --> 01:00:16.175
‎My last surgery‎…

681
01:00:16.759 --> 01:00:18.386
‎They're inducing the donor now.

682
01:00:19.929 --> 01:00:21.222
‎Let's begin.

683
01:00:38.364 --> 01:00:40.867
‎Second surgeries always have ‎more adhesions to deal with.

684
01:00:41.617 --> 01:00:43.911
‎Keep us posted so we can stay on schedule.

685
01:00:43.995 --> 01:00:44.954
‎Yes, Doctor.

686
01:00:46.080 --> 01:00:49.000
‎You're playing music today, Dr. Jo?

687
01:00:49.500 --> 01:00:50.334
‎Yes.

688
01:00:50.418 --> 01:00:54.255
‎The patient asked for songs ‎and ambient sounds he liked.

689
01:01:25.536 --> 01:01:26.412
‎Oh, Dad!

690
01:01:28.831 --> 01:01:30.041
‎Hello.

691
01:01:31.584 --> 01:01:32.877
‎May the children's nightmares‎…

692
01:01:35.671 --> 01:01:36.506
‎their screams…

693
01:01:48.226 --> 01:01:49.143
‎and their pain…

694
01:01:52.939 --> 01:01:54.065
‎follow you to your bed.

695
01:02:14.335 --> 01:02:19.507
‎FLUMAZENIL: A REVERSAL AGENT USED ‎TO WAKE A PATIENT FROM CERTAIN SEDATIVES

696
01:02:19.590 --> 01:02:21.300
‎You can no longer rest in peace.

697
01:02:32.603 --> 01:02:34.021
‎This is your hell.

698
01:02:36.023 --> 01:02:37.775
‎Beginning dissection. Bovie.

699
01:04:00.232 --> 01:04:03.152
‎DOCTOR X: MAFIA IN WHITE

700
01:04:42.274 --> 01:04:45.194
‎DOCTOR X: MAFIA IN WHITE

701
01:04:45.277 --> 01:04:47.655
‎He's just not that kind of person.

702
01:04:48.447 --> 01:04:50.616
‎But that's not the case for me.

703
01:04:52.034 --> 01:04:53.119
‎Closing the hospital?

704
01:04:53.202 --> 01:04:54.203
‎Damn it!

705
01:04:54.912 --> 01:04:56.747
‎Somehow we both survived

706
01:04:56.831 --> 01:04:58.332
‎and made it all the way here.

707
01:04:59.250 --> 01:05:00.876
‎You're done being a doctor after this!

708
01:05:00.960 --> 01:05:02.461
‎Do you believe in God?

709
01:05:03.713 --> 01:05:04.547
‎I hate God.

710
01:05:05.423 --> 01:05:06.382
‎I'm stopping

711
01:05:07.550 --> 01:05:08.384
‎the surgery.

712
01:05:10.928 --> 01:05:15.933
‎Subtitle translation by: Jenny Kim
